= Glossary

#table(
  columns: (auto, 1fr),
  table.header([Term], [Definition]),
  [*AE*], [Anniversary Edition — the Fallout 4 runtime branch starting at game version 1.11.137, culminating in 1.11.221 (May 27, 2026), this guide's target version.],
  [*AWKCR*], [Armor and Weapon Keywords Community Resource — a legacy shared-keyword framework many older armor mods required; largely superseded by standalone mods like Armorsmith Extended v7.0+.],
  [*ESP / ESM / ESL*], [Plugin file types Fallout 4 loads: ESM (master, foundational), ESP (plugin, standard mod), ESL (light plugin, uses a smaller ID range so more can be loaded at once).],
  [*F4SE*], [Fallout 4 Script Extender — a modder's resource that extends the Papyrus scripting engine's capabilities without modifying the game executable.],
  [*FOMOD*], [A packaged mod installer format with a step-by-step options wizard, supported natively by Mod Organizer 2.],
  [*Legendary Enemy*], [An enemy marked with a star icon on its health bar; always drops a Legendary-quality weapon or armor piece on death.],
  [*LOOT*], [Load Order Optimisation Tool — sorts plugin load order automatically based on community-maintained masterlist rules; built into MO2 2.5's Plugins tab.],
  [*Load Order*], [The sequence in which plugins (ESM/ESP/ESL files) are read by the game engine; later-loaded plugins override earlier ones for the same records.],
  [*MCM*], [Mod Configuration Menu — an in-game settings screen (accessed from the pause menu) that mods hook into instead of shipping ad-hoc configuration tools.],
  [*MO2*], [Mod Organizer 2 — a virtual file system mod manager that keeps every mod isolated until merged at runtime, leaving the base game files untouched.],
  [*NG*], [Next-Gen — the Fallout 4 runtime branch starting at game version 1.10.984 (2024), preceding the Anniversary Edition (AE).],
  [*OG*], [Old-Gen — the original, pre-2024 Fallout 4 runtime, version 1.10.163 and earlier.],
  [*Papyrus*], [Fallout 4's built-in scripting language, used for quests, mod logic, and gameplay systems.],
  [*Perk*], [A gameplay bonus unlocked with level-up points, gated behind a SPECIAL attribute's rank (e.g. the Gunslinger perk requires a minimum Agility score).],
  [*Precombine / Previs*], [Engine-level optimization data (precombined meshes and previsibility/occlusion culling) that lets the game render busy areas efficiently; scrapping/building mods can break this data unless a compatible patch (e.g. a Previsibines Repair Pack build) exists.],
  [*Provisioner*], [A settler assigned to walk a supply line between two settlements, sharing workshop resources between them; requires the Local Leader perk to assign.],
  [*SPECIAL*], [The seven core character attributes: Strength, Perception, Endurance, Charisma, Intelligence, Agility, Luck.],
  [*V.A.T.S.*], [Vault-Tec Assisted Targeting System — a tactical time-slow targeting mode that spends Action Points to queue precise, chance-based attacks.],
  [*Workshop / Settlement Mode*], [The build interface used to place structures, furniture, and defenses within a settlement's workshop boundary.],
)

